SUMMARY:Survivalist Series: Introduction to Camp Skills
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/intro-bushcraft)**\n\n**Be
 hold the profound utility of plants!**\n\nLong before rope\, tools\, and c
 onstruction materials came off a shelf\, it came from the land: twisted fr
 om roots\, stripped from bark\, and spun from plant fiber.\n\nThis one-day
  workshop introduces you to the concepts of bushcraft\, how to source raw 
 materials straight from the wild and how to make them into things you need
  to survive. You'll learn to see the forest differently and walk away with
  the skills (and a few finished pieces) to prove it.\n\n**You will learn:*
 *\n\n* How to identify and ethically harvest plants\n* How to process thes
 e materials to create survival essentials\n* Basic structures and tools th
 at can be easily built\, to improve wilderness convenience and quality of 
 life.\n* How to apply bushcraft concepts to meal preparation and cooking.\
 n* The principles of sustainable bushcraft: what to take\, what to leave\,
  and how to harvest without depleting the source\n\n**Who It's For**: Anyo
 ne looking to build on their outdoor skills with hands-on\, practical craf
 t. No prior experience required\, though this pairs well with our Foraging
  workshop for those looking to round out their plant knowledge.\n\n**About
  this Series**: The Survivalist Series is an expert-led set of courses des
 igned to develop applicable and life-saving skills in the outdoors. Keep y
 our eyes peeled for more courses on many other topics as they become avail
 able.\n\n**Highlights**\n**Plant Fiber Cordage:** Twist raw fiber into cor
 dage strong enough to lash a shelter frame or hang a pack. And you will be
  able to bring some home!\n**Ethical Harvesting:** Learn to read a plant b
 efore you touch it\, and how much you can take without setting the populat
 ion back.\n**Expert Instruction:** Your amazing expert guide will teach yo
 u everything you need to know in a safe and approachable way.\n\n**Event c
 ost: $80+HST (for explorer members) - $30 optional transport available.**\
 n**Register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/intro-bushc
 raft)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate abou
 t building an outdoors community that connects you to the life-changing ma
 gic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\n\nMembers range from 
 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto
  from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't refl
 ect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community member
 s at each event. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but small e
 nough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [www.wil
 dernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
